  "visualBrief": "Temple of Caesar present-day medium-fi exterior: surviving concrete/brick podium and isolated eroded cores, low return/foundation traces, curved altar recess, broad protective canopy with timber understructure, rough altar blocks, a few fallen marble fragments and low visitor rail. No intact ancient colonnade or temple roof is reconstructed. Adjacent Arch of Augustus, Regia, Vesta, Antoninus and Faustina and the wider Forum remain independent.",
